Daimon::initialize
├── given a root set of two or more schemes
│   └── it should install every scheme and seed each validator's signer
├── given a root set smaller than two schemes
│   └── it should revert with RootSetTooSmall
├── given validators and initDatas of different lengths
│   └── it should revert with LengthMismatch
├── given an already-initialized account
│   └── it should revert (owner already set)
├── given the single-argument initialize(address)
│   └── it should revert with NotSupported
└── given an already-initialized account and a second initialize carrying a genesis mandate
    └── it should revert (once-only) and never bind the injected mandate post-deploy
